- The provided excerpts do not show explicit restatements or post-balance-sheet events that change revenue/gross profit numbers in the provided sections. The Prospectus does mention forecasts and sensitivity due to COVID-19 and impairment testing indicators. The Annual Report includes an Auditor’s Report expressing an unmodified opinion — no restatement mentioned in the auditor excerpt included.

---

### 3. Additional context (if relevant):

1) Units and minor differences:
- Both Prospectus and Annual Report use thousands of NOK (NOKk / NOK 1000). When assembling a side-by-side table, ensure both use the same unit (NOKk) — Annual Report "Amounts in NOK 1000" equals Prospectus "NOKk".
- There is a small difference in YE 2019 revenue reported in the Prospectus (2,932,707 NOKk) vs the Annual Report (2,890,025 NOKk). However, computed gross profit for YE 2019 from both documents is essentially identical (~752,900 NOKk). The Prospectus explicitly warns about differences in reporting entity and comparability, which likely explains this difference. I flagged this in the detailed section above.

2) Where pro forma or adjusted figures appear:
- The Annual Report contains explicit Adjusted EBITDA reconciliation (Operating profit → EBITDA → addbacks → Adjusted EBITDA) with numeric details (see extracted reconciliation). Adjusted EBITDA margin (11.0% in 2020) is provided on operating revenues.
- The Prospectus defines the same APMs and provides forecast ranges (management outlook) for full-year 2020 revenue and gross margin, and points to reconciliation sections (10.7) for APMs. The provided Prospectus excerpts include interim statements and definitions but do not include a detailed pro forma adjusted reconciliation table in the supplied excerpts beyond APM definitions and the interim condensed statement. The Annual Report does include the reconciliation.

3) What I could not find in the provided excerpts:
- A detailed pro forma adjusted revenue reconciliation (e.g., pro forma revenue after acquisitions, or separate adjusted revenue lines) beyond the Adjusted EBITDA reconciliation in the Annual Report. The Prospectus refers to Section 10.7 for Non-IFRS measures reconciliation — that section was not included in the provided excerpts, so I could not extract a complete reconciliation table from Prospectus (beyond definitions and forecasts).
- Any explicit restatements or subsequent events changing reported historical revenue/gross profit numbers were not present in the supplied excerpts. If there are appendices or later sections (e.g., Section 10.7 in the Prospectus or the full note package in Appendix C) they were not included; they may contain further reconciliations or pro forma adjustments.

4) Suggested next steps if you want a formatted deliverable:
- I can produce a side-by-side table (CSV or structured list) containing:
  - Columns: Period / Document / Revenue (NOKk) / Direct cost of services rendered (NOKk) / Computed Gross profit (NOKk) / Gross margin (%) / Source & excerpt reference (Prospectus page/section or Annual Report note).
  - Rows: YE 2019 (Prospectus), YE 2019 (Annual Report), YTD 2020 (Prospectus half-year), FY 2020 (Annual Report), and Prospectus forecast (2020 range/expected gross margin).
- If you require the exact page numbers in the original PDF, I will need the full documents with their page numbering or the explicit page references beyond the excerpt headers. The excerpts here include internal numbering (e.g., "Copyright 2020 LINK Mobility. All rights reserved. 2") but not reliable PDF page numbers for every excerpt. If you provide the full PDFs or confirm you want the references as "Prospectus - Section X / excerpt Y" and "Annual Report - Note / excerpt", I will include them.

5) Final note on comparability:
- The Prospectus itself warns that comparisons across years are limited due to (a) changes in reporting entity (Link Mobility Group AS vs the new parent after takeover in Oct 2018), and (b) extensive M&A activity. Use caution when comparing 2017/2018/2019 and intra-year interim figures vs the full-year Annual Report figures. The Annual Report’s Adjusted EBITDA reconciliation is useful to compare operating performance excluding acquisition and one-time items.

